# class: adr
# schema: id | title | status | summary | source
# source-glob: docs/adr/*.md
# recipe: builtin:adr
# reindexed: 2026-05-23 (added ADR-0008 / ADR-0009 / ADR-0010; updated ADR-0005 status)

ADR-0001 | Per-service topology derivation — five-pass algorithm on the read side | accepted | Topology derived read-side per request via five-pass algorithm (bucket-by-env, explicit-first, correlation-fallback, merge, dangling); no stored topology rows | @docs/adr/ADR-0001-topology-derivation-five-pass.md
ADR-0002 | Modular monolith — single API container hosting two library surfaces | superseded by ADR-0006 (2026-05-19) | Co-location mechanics retained as historical record: one ASP.NET host (backend/api/) composes write-api/ + read-api/ libraries + shared/; single Dockerfile; X-Api-Key on Write group only; future split is host+gateway-config change. Framing reset by ADR-0006 (microservices architecture; co-location is a packaging choice) | @docs/adr/ADR-0002-modular-monolith-consolidation.md
ADR-0003 | Theme persistence in localStorage with FOIT-safe inline bootstrap | accepted | Theme preference in localStorage.dashboard.theme; FOIT-safe inline-script bootstrap before SPA boot sets <html data-theme>; single writer post-bootstrap (ThemeService in frontend/shared/) | @docs/adr/ADR-0003-theme-persistence-and-foit-safe-bootstrap.md
ADR-0004 | Opaque per-progress_reporter cursor; backend-held; out-of-process fetcher; plug-in adapter shape | accepted (paired with CR-0009) | 4 decisions: (1) cursor lives on backend not fetcher container via GET/PUT /api/fetcher/state/{source-id}; (2) cursor is opaque per-progress_reporter blob VARCHAR(4096) keyed by (progress_reporter, source_id) - backend never parses; (3) fetcher runs in separate container (Dashboard.Fetcher.Host) not in-process BackgroundService (NFR-05 preservation + opt-in + failure isolation + credential isolation; minReplicas=maxReplicas=1 when enabled); (4) ICiCdAdapter plug-in shape with AdapterId + FetchPageAsync(sourceId, opaqueCursor, pageSize, ct) -> (events, newCursor, hasMore); host owns scheduler/retry/back-off/Write-API dispatch | @docs/adr/ADR-0004-opaque-per-progress-reporter-cursor.md
ADR-0005 | Release-install migration actuation via tag-pinned migration.sql release asset | superseded by ADR-0009 (2026-05-22) | Historical record: Release installer pulled tag-pinned migration.sql GitHub Release asset and applied via one-shot postgres:16-alpine container (profile-gated, default-on); idempotent contract; no source tree / SDK on install host; local-dev SDK+bind-mount flow unchanged. Entire external-migrations model retired by ADR-0009 (API host self-migrates on startup) | @docs/adr/ADR-0005-release-install-migration-actuation.md
ADR-0006 | Microservices architecture with container co-location of Write + Read API services | accepted (2026-05-19) — supersedes ADR-0002 | Reframes the backend architecture: project is microservices (Write API, Read API, Fetcher, Frontend SPA, Gateway — distinct services with distinct concerns); Write + Read API services co-located in deployment-dashboard-api image for operational simplicity within NFR-02; co-location is a packaging choice, not the architecture itself. Zero code/infra/Dockerfile change; ADR-0002 co-location mechanics + future-split trigger conditions survive as historical record. Frontend "modular monolith" Angular-workspace wording is a different concept (Angular libraries pattern) and stays | @docs/adr/ADR-0006-microservices-architecture-with-container-co-location.md
ADR-0007 | Vendor adapters convert vendor correlation signals into parent_deployments edges; read-side five-pass remains backstop | accepted (2026-05-20) — paired with issue #19; amends CR-0009 §3d endpoint list | 3 rules for vendor adapters (today GHA; tomorrow ADO/Jenkins/GitLab/CircleCI): (1) convert what the vendor asserts (e.g. GHA needs: DAG between deployment-producing jobs + per-(service,environment) cursor-ordered predecessor) — not what the vendor only renders (e.g. same-sha grouping; defer to read-side ADR-0001 pass 3 which has per-request correlationAttribute + per-service override visibility the fetcher lacks); (2) on signal-unrecovery (API 404/5xx after retry, YAML parse failure), emit no edge from the affected signal + INFO log + cycle continues — timing inference between parallel jobs explicitly rejected because parallel-job ordering is ambiguous and a fabricated edge blocks read-side pass 3 correction; (3) ADR-0001 five-pass remains live + unchanged — pass 2 (explicit-first) consumes adapter-emitted edges identically to push-mode-emitted ones; pass 3 (correlation fallback) bypasses events with explicit edges; passes 1/4/5 unaffected. No wire-shape change (parent_deployments already exists per CR-0003). Per-adapter endpoint-budget growth must be documented in the adapter's owning CR (CR-0009 §3d for GHA — amended in parallel: GET /actions/runs/{id} run metadata for path+head_sha + GET /actions/runs/{id}/jobs + GET /contents/.github/workflows/{path}?ref={head_sha}; all three cacheable per cycle; YAML fetched at run revision so a later YAML edit on default branch does not change the needs: attributed to a past run). Implementation tracked under issue #19 | @docs/adr/ADR-0007-vendor-adapters-emit-parent-deployments.md
ADR-0008 | Leaky-bucket cap on observed remaining; re-publish-on-tick (no persistence); per-token cap with per-(adapter, source-id) reporting | accepted (paired with CR-0011) | 4 decisions: (1) cap accounting is leaky-bucket on upstream-observed Remaining (skip-request := upstream_used >= SelfImposedCap AND now < upstream_reset_at; no fetcher-side counter; restart-safe); (2) reporting topology is in-memory ConcurrentDictionary per API process + re-publish-on-tick — no persistence, no Redis, no new EF entity; recovered within one poll interval after replica restart (NFR-05 + NFR-02 preserved); (3) cap scope is per upstream token (= per adapter instance); reporting stays per-(adapter_id, source_id) so dashboard shows per-repo rows; (4) upstream_used field is observed not counted — derived as upstream_limit - upstream_remaining, counting all callers of the PAT | @docs/adr/ADR-0008-leaky-bucket-cap-and-republish-on-tick.md
ADR-0009 | API host applies EF migrations on startup; external migrations service + migration.sql release asset retired | accepted (paired with issue #22) — supersedes ADR-0005 | API host calls Database.Migrate() between app.Build() and app.Run() via DashboardDbContext temporary scope; failure aborts process with LogLevel.Critical before app.Run() (loud failure vs silent unmigrated-DB failure mode of ADR-0005). Retires: dev_env + release compose migrations service, install.ps1 -SkipMigrations flag, migration.sql release asset, emit-migration-artefact workflow plumbing. Concurrent replicas race-safely via __EFMigrationsHistory unique-constraint (NFR-05 preserved). No Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Design reference needed at runtime (Design pkg is tooling-only). Startup overhead: 5-30 s first apply per schema version; sub-second thereafter | @docs/adr/ADR-0009-startup-applied-ef-migrations.md
ADR-0010 | dev_env/docker-compose.local.yml layered on install/docker-compose.release.yml via Compose merge | accepted (2026-05-22, paired with issue #21) | Override file carries only 3 contributor-flow deltas (build: blocks + dev-literal env-var substitutions + pgadmin convenience service) + pull_policy: never; release file is the canonical service inventory; contributor invocation is docker compose -f install/docker-compose.release.yml -f dev_env/docker-compose.local.yml up -d --build; -Scaled stack stays standalone (single-file); cosmetic stderr warnings on variable interpolation accepted (vs env-file violation of zero-setup invariant). Structurally eliminates drift between release + contributor compose files | @docs/adr/ADR-0010-dev-env-compose-derives-from-release.md
